---
id: org.dxos.plugin.inbox
name: InboxPlugin
version: 0.2.0
---

Unified inbox plugin for `DXOS` Composer — email, calendar, and contacts in one place, surfaced
alongside workspace content. Mail syncs from multiple providers (Google/Gmail and JMAP, e.g.
Fastmail) into an append-only feed; calendar and contacts sync from Google. AI extractors, a
cursored processing pipeline, and an enrichment cascade derive structured objects, summaries,
classifications, and RDF facts from message content.

Entry points: `plugin.tsx` (browser), `plugin.node.ts` (skills/ops/schema only), and
`plugin.workerd.ts` (ops + schema — lets EDGE run sync remotely).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document. The standard terms are defined in the
Appendix; the app terms (`node`, `deck`, `plank`, `companion`, `surface`, `menu`) are defined in
[`packages/reflect/deus/lang/app.mdl`](../../reflect/deus/lang/app.mdl) (`org.dxos.spec.app`).

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`     |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`        |
| `node`      | `org.dxos.mdl.node@1.0`        |
| `deck`      | `org.dxos.mdl.deck@1.0`        |
| `plank`     | `org.dxos.mdl.plank@1.0`       |
| `companion` | `org.dxos.mdl.companion@1.0`   |
| `surface`   | `org.dxos.mdl.surface@1.0`     |
| `menu`      | `org.dxos.mdl.menu@1.0`        |

## External types

- `Message`, `DraftMessage`, `Event`, `Person`, `Organization` — `@dxos/types`. Messages/events
  live in feeds; people/organizations in the space. A `DraftMessage` is an unsent `Message`,
  distinguished by its own instance check rather than by a field.
- `Feed`, `Tag`, `TagIndex` — `@dxos/echo` / `@dxos/schema`. Feed members are immutable; mutable
  tag membership lives in the mailbox's `TagIndex` sidecar.
- `Cursor` (`@dxos/link`) — the sync **binding**: an external cursor whose `spec.target` is the
  Mailbox/Calendar and whose `spec.source` is the provider access token. Carries sync options and
  durable window/delta state.
- `Connection`, `ConnectorSpec` — `@dxos/plugin-connector`. Provider credentials and the connector
  registry (materialize/sync/trigger declarations live in plugin-google / plugin-jmap).
- `Instructions`, `Project` — `@dxos/compute`. Reply guidance; extracted project objects.
- `Fact` / `FactStore` — `@dxos/pipeline-rdf`.

## Types

```mdl
type Mailbox
  desc: |
    The mail container: a named handle onto an append-only message feed plus its mutable
    sidecars. Declares its deck level chain and its skills.
  fields:
    name?: string
    feed: Ref<Feed>              # immutable synced messages
    tags: Ref<TagIndex>          # mutable tag membership for feed members
    annotations?: Ref<Feed>      # lazy append-only feed of derived summaries
    instructions?: Ref<Instructions>   # reply-drafting guidance
    extractors?: { enabled: boolean, threshold?: number }
    messageFilters?: MessageFilter[]   # exclusion rules ("ignore sender")
    filters?: SavedFilter[]      # saved UI query filters {name, filter}
    subscriptions?: Subscription[]     # derived bulk-mail senders
    extracted?: Record<messageId, objectIds>  # extraction provenance record
```

```mdl
type SavedFilter
  desc: A saved, named query string surfacing as a folder node under the mailbox.
  fields:
    name: string
    filter: string               # query expression (tag/text grammar)
```

```mdl
type MessageFilter
  desc: An exclusion rule dropped messages must match (currently a `from` regex).
  fields:
    from: string
```

```mdl
type SystemTags
  desc: |
    Canonical, provider-agnostic tag registry: starred | inbox | important | sent | draft |
    personal | social | promotions | updates | forums | spam. Each provider maps its own
    vocabulary onto these, so a Gmail star and a JMAP $flagged resolve to the same Tag object.
    Supersedes the legacy MessageState enum. Membership helpers operate over the container's
    TagIndex (feed members carry no meta.tags of their own).
```

```mdl
type Calendar
  desc: Calendar container — same feed + tags shape as Mailbox; no deck chain.
  fields:
    name?: string
    feed: Ref<Feed>
    tags: Ref<TagIndex>
```

```mdl
type DraftEvent
  desc: |
    Not a schema — a convention with helpers: a space-db Event parented to its Calendar with no
    provider foreign key is a draft; saving it creates the remote event and the next sync
    reconciles it.
```

```mdl
type ExtractedFrom
  desc: Provenance relation extracted-object → source Message.
  fields:
    extractorId: string
    extractedAt: string
    confidence?: number
```

```mdl
type SentTag
  desc: |
    Foreign key of the tag the provider's own copy of a sent message will carry (Gmail's SENT
    label, or the JMAP account's Sent folder resolved by role). `label` is a fallback used only
    before the first sync has seen the tag.
  fields:
    source: string
    id: string
    label: string
```

```mdl
type MailSend
  desc: Provider-agnostic send contract, routed via the MailSendOperation capability by connector id.
  fields:
    input: { message: Message, connection: Connection }
    output: { id: string, threadId?: string, sentTag?: SentTag }
```

```mdl
type Settings
  desc: KVS-backed plugin settings.
  fields:
    conversations?: boolean      # group messages into threads (default true)
    loadRemoteImages?: boolean   # default false (tracking pixels)
```

```mdl
type SyncOptions
  desc: Per-binding sync options stored on the Cursor spec.
  fields:
    syncBackDays?: number
    syncForwardDays?: number     # calendar only
    filter?: string
```

```mdl
type SyncStreamConfig
  desc: Per-provider pipeline tuning (page sizes, fetch concurrency, run caps, date chunking).
```

Capability tags (`InboxCapabilities`): `Settings` (writable atom), `ObjectExtractor` (multi —
contact + summarize extractors contributed here; other plugins may add more), `MailboxAction`
(injected toolbar actions, e.g. plugin-brain's Analyze), `MailSendOperation` (provider send op
keyed by connector id).

## App graph

Node paths: space → `communications` group → `mailboxes` section → mailbox → child segments.
System-tag views are pre-seeded, non-removable filter nodes — the same mechanism as saved user
filters.

```mdl
node MailboxesSection
  desc: Nav-tree section shown when any Mailbox exists in the space.
  source: node:SpaceRoot
  properties:
    id: mailboxes
    icon: ph--tray--regular
  actions: [op:AddMailbox]
```

```mdl
node MailboxNode
  desc: |
    One node per Mailbox. The node itself is the Inbox view (filter '#inbox'); children are
    filter views over the same mailbox subject, so every folder opens MailboxArticle with
    different filter/systemTag props.
  source: node:MailboxesSection
  subject: type:Mailbox
  properties:
    role: branch
    filter: '#inbox'
    systemTag: inbox
  children:
    - AllMail        # filter ''
    - Sent           # filter '#sent', systemTag sent
    - Drafts         # filter '', systemTag draft; action: op:DraftEmailAndOpen
    - Subscriptions  # bulk-mail senders view (own article)
    - SavedFilters   # one node per mailbox.filters entry; actions: op:RenameFilter, delete
  actions: [op:GoogleMailSync, op:EnrichMailbox, op:ProcessMailbox, op:ResetFeedCursor]
```

```mdl
node MessageNodes
  desc: |
    Every feed message (and mailbox-scoped draft) as a hidden child of its mailbox — deep-link
    resolution only, never shown in the nav tree. Data is the Echo object, so messages pick up
    the standard object companions (assistant, properties, debug) contributed by other plugins.
  source: node:MailboxNode
  subject: type:Message
  properties:
    disposition: hidden
```

```mdl
node CalendarNode
  desc: Standard type section for Calendar; events (and draft events) as hidden children.
  source: node:SpaceRoot
  subject: type:Calendar
  children:
    - EventNodes     # hidden, deep-link resolution only
  actions: [op:GoogleCalendarSync]
```

The sync action appears only when an external `Cursor` targets the mailbox/calendar and a matching
`Connection` exists; its spinner/disabled state reads the `#sync` progress monitor.

## Deck

```mdl
deck MailboxDeck
  desc: |
    Declared on the Mailbox schema (DeckAnnotation). Reading a mailbox is a chain: opening a
    message replaces the message plank rather than growing the deck, and picking a different
    message drops the attachment that belonged to the last one. Meta/ctrl-click opts out and
    opens a free plank. The attachment level is declared but not yet opened by any container.
  chain: MailboxPlank > MessagePlank > AttachmentPlank  # AttachmentPlank: declared level, no plank yet
```

```mdl
plank MailboxPlank
  subject: type:Mailbox
  article: component:MailboxArticle
```

```mdl
plank MessagePlank
  subject: type:Message
  article: component:MessageArticle
  parent: MailboxPlank
```

## Companions

This plugin contributes **no companion nodes of its own** — message/event children are ordinary
hidden nodes, not companions. Companions appearing on inbox objects come from generic
every-object contributors: plugin-space (properties/info), plugin-assistant (chat),
plugin-routine (automations — consuming this plugin's Routine templates), plugin-debug. The
mailbox's create-topic action reveals a `topic` companion contributed externally.

What this plugin does handle is **companion-mode rendering**: `MessageArticle`/`EventArticle`
accept `companionTo` (the scoping mailbox/calendar, resolved from the graph) and show an
"open as primary" toolbar action.

