```

```mdl
surface EventCardSurface
  role: cardContent
  subject: type:Event
  component: component:EventCard
```

```mdl
surface PropertiesSurfaces
  role: objectProperties
  subject: type:Mailbox | type:Calendar
  component: component:MailboxProperties | component:CalendarProperties
```

```mdl
surface SaveFilterPopoverSurface
  role: popover
  component: component:SaveFilterPopover
```

```mdl
surface RelatedSurfaces
  role: related
  subject: type:Person | type:Organization
  component: component:RelatedToContact | component:RelatedToOrganization
```

## Menus

```mdl
menu MailboxToolbar
  of: type:Mailbox
  disposition: toolbar
  items:
    - op:GoogleMailSync        # sync (spinner from #sync monitor)
    - op:EnrichMailbox         # enrich / stop
    - sort, load-remote-images # view toggles (settings-backed)
    - extract group            # ObjectExtractor + injected MailboxAction contributions
    - op:DraftEmailAndOpen     # compose
    - filter                   # search box slot (hidden in Drafts view)
```

```mdl
menu MailboxContextMenu
  of: node:MailboxNode
  disposition: list-item
  items: [op:GoogleMailSync, op:EnrichMailbox, op:ProcessMailbox, op:ResetFeedCursor]
```

```mdl
menu SavedFilterMenu
  of: node:MailboxNode          # saved-filter child nodes
  disposition: list-item
  items: [op:RenameFilter, delete-filter]
```

## Components

Containers (surface-bound, lazy). Presentation state (selection, tags, stars) rides atoms; feed
reads are paginated.

```mdl
component MailboxArticle
  desc: |
    Paged, thread-grouped message list over the feed (whole-thread semi-join), with filter
    editor (tag/text grammar, save-as-filter), per-tile tag chips + star toggle, toolbar
    (menu:MailboxToolbar), and a statusbar ProgressMeter for whichever of sync/process/enrich
    is active. Empty state: InitializeMailbox (connect an account).
  props: { subject: Mailbox, filter?: string, systemTag?: SystemTagId }
```

```mdl
component MessageArticle
  desc: |
    Conversation (thread) detail: message tiles over a combined space+feed query by threadId,
    summaries from the annotations feed, AI reply, delete, open-as-plank.
  props: { subject: Message, companionTo?: Mailbox }
```

```mdl
component EditMessageArticle
  desc: Draft composer — subject/to/body editor, send via contributed MailSendOperation, AI generate-reply.
  props: { subject: DraftMessage }
```

```mdl
component CalendarArticle
  desc: Calendar grid + event list with range selection; InitializeCalendar empty state.
  props: { subject: Calendar }
```

```mdl
component EventArticle
  desc: Event detail/editor; draft events are editable and savable (creates the remote event).
  props: { subject: Event, companionTo?: Calendar }
```

```mdl
component SubscriptionsArticle
  desc: Bulk-mail subscription list (sender, count); select + unsubscribe.
  props: { subject: Mailbox }
```

Supporting: `MessageCard` / `EventCard` (card bodies), `MailboxProperties` / `CalendarProperties`
(object-properties panels: sync toggle/trigger), `SaveFilterPopover` (names a filter into
`mailbox.filters`), `RelatedToContact` / `RelatedToOrganization` (related messages/events/people),
`InitializeMailbox` / `InitializeCalendar` (connect flows).

## Services

```mdl
service MailSyncProvider
  desc: |
    Effect service each mail provider implements (gmail in plugin-google, jmap in plugin-jmap):
    name, SyncStreamConfig, foreignKeySource, and prepare(preparation) → source stream. The
    provider yields pages + reconciles; the harness owns everything else (see Sync).
  loading: lazy
```

```mdl
service FactStore
  desc: Space-level RDF fact store (from @dxos/pipeline-rdf); AnalyzeMailbox writes extracted facts here.
```

## Operations

Keys `org.dxos.operation.inbox.<name>`. Provider-facing ops are defined here but handled in
plugin-google / plugin-jmap; `GenerateReply` is handled in plugin-brain. Long-running mailbox
pipelines report through progress monitors keyed `<mailbox uri>#<suffix>` (`sync`, `process`,
`enrich`, `classify`, `summarize`, `analyze`, `correspondents`, `subscriptions`) and serialize on
a per-mailbox lock.

### Sync (provider-handled)

```mdl
op GoogleMailSync
  desc: Sync Gmail into the mailbox feed via the shared harness. Idempotent; resumable; capped.
  input: { binding: Ref<Cursor> }
  output: { newMessages: number }
```

```mdl
op JmapSync
  desc: Same contract for JMAP (Fastmail).
  input: { binding: Ref<Cursor> }
  output: { newMessages: number }
```

```mdl
op GoogleCalendarSync
  desc: Sync Google Calendar events into the calendar feed (windowed; separate from the mail harness).
  input: { binding: Ref<Cursor> }
  output: { newEvents: number }
```

```mdl
op GoogleContactsSync
  desc: Sync a Google contact group into space Person objects (upserts).
  output: { upserted: number }
```

`MaterializeGmailTarget` / `MaterializeJmapTarget` / `MaterializeCalendarTarget` create the local
Mailbox/Calendar before a cursor exists; `GetGoogleCalendars` / `GetGoogleContactGroups` discover
remote targets. All are ConnectorSpec plumbing.

### Compose & send

```mdl
op DraftEmail
  desc: Agent-facing draft creation (subject/to/body/replyTo).
  output: { newMessageDXN: DXN }
```

```mdl
op DraftEmailAndOpen
  desc: Create a draft (compose | reply | reply-all | forward) and open it as a plank.
```

```mdl
op GmailSend
  desc: Send a draft via Gmail; JmapSend is the JMAP counterpart. Routed by connector id.
  input: MailSend.Input
  output: MailSend.Output
```

```mdl
op CreateGoogleCalendarEvent
  desc: Write counterpart of calendar sync — creates the remote event for a saved draft event.
```

### Extract, classify, enrich

```mdl
op ExtractMessage
  desc: Dispatch one message to the best-matching ObjectExtractor; persist results + ExtractedFrom provenance.
```

```mdl
op EnrichMailbox
  desc: |
    Cascade orchestrator over tiers deterministic → classify → summarize → analyze (default:
    first three). Idempotent; per-stage results; cancellable via the #enrich monitor.
```

```mdl
op ProcessMailbox
  desc: Cursored processing pipeline over the feed (durable consumer cursor); ResetFeedCursor rewinds it.
```

Constituents (each idempotent, capped, individually invocable): `ClassifyEmail` /
`ClassifyMailbox` (AI tagging, spam + category, known-Person short-circuit), `SummarizeMailbox`
(per-contact summaries into the annotations feed), `AnalyzeMailbox` (RDF facts into FactStore),
`ExtractCorrespondents` (Person/Organization for people the user wrote to),
`ExtractSubscriptions` (List-Unsubscribe scan → mailbox.subscriptions),
`ExtractContactFromMessage` / `ExtractSummaryFromMessage` (pure extract, no writes),
`CreateProjectFromMessage` (thread → Project with LLM summary), `GenerateReply` (grounded reply
draft; handled in plugin-brain). `ExtractContact` and `ExtractMailbox` are deprecated.

### Misc & navigation

```mdl
op ReadEmail
  desc: Agent tool — read mailbox content as text (skip/limit).
```

`AddMailbox` (create-object flow), `RenameFilter` (saved-filter node action),
`ResetFeedCursor` (rewinds a named consumer's durable cursor over the feed),
`UnsubscribeSender` (adds a skip-sender filter and fires the RFC 8058 one-click endpoint).

## Sync

`runMailSync` (subpath export `@dxos/plugin-inbox/sync`, no React) is the provider-agnostic
harness: it loads binding → mailbox → feed → tag index, resolves date windows and delta tokens
from the durable `Cursor`, streams provider pages through dedup → cap → decode, merges provider
reconciles (retag/delete by foreign id), runs the shared email tail (attachments → contacts →
draft reconciliation → stats → commit units), commits in groups, reports progress (`#sync`
monitor), and schedules itself again (`runAgain`) while capped or behind delta. Scheduling policy
is domain-owned: 10-minute cron, auto-sync on, remote (EDGE) on. Provider `MailSyncProvider`
layers live in plugin-google and plugin-jmap; calendar/contacts sync are separate plugin-google
handlers.

Routine templates (`automation-templates.ts`): hourly `processMailbox` and daily `enrichMailbox`
runnables, disabled by default, surfaced in the automations companion.

## Skills

- **Inbox** (`org.dxos.skill.inbox`, agent-enableable; attached to Mailbox via SkillsAnnotation) —
  mailbox management: ClassifyEmail, DraftEmail, ReadEmail, GoogleMailSync, ExtractMessage.
- **Inbox Send** (`org.dxos.skill.inboxSend`) — send-only companion: GmailSend.
- **Calendar** (`org.dxos.skill.calendar`; attached to Calendar) — GoogleCalendarSync.

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Mailbox
  req F-1.1: Messages sync into an append-only feed; the article lists them paged and
    thread-grouped, newest first, interactive during initial sync (no empty-state flash).
  req F-1.2: Tags, stars, and read state live in the TagIndex sidecar keyed by canonical
    SystemTags; providers map their vocabularies onto them.
  req F-1.3: System-tag folders (inbox, all-mail, sent, drafts) and saved user filters are
    filter nodes over the same mailbox subject.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Reading chain
  req F-2.1: Opening a message from the mailbox reuses the message-level plank (deck chain);
    meta/ctrl-click opens a free plank instead.
  req F-2.2: Message and event nodes resolve deep links but stay hidden in the nav tree.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Provider sync
  req F-3.1: Sync is idempotent, resumable, capped per run, and cancellable; progress reports
    via the #sync monitor and the mailbox statusbar.
  req F-3.2: A provider is a MailSyncProvider layer; adding one requires no harness changes.
  req F-3.3: Sync runs on EDGE (workerd entry) on a 10-minute cron when enabled.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Compose & send
  req F-4.1: Drafts are local DraftMessages scoped to the mailbox; send routes through the
    provider's MailSendOperation and the sent copy reconciles on next sync.
  req F-4.2: AI reply drafting is grounded on the thread and extracted facts.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Calendar & draft events
  req F-5.1: Events sync into the calendar feed; draft events are local Events parented to the
    calendar and become remote events on save.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Extraction & enrichment
  req F-6.1: Extractors are contributed capabilities; extraction records ExtractedFrom provenance.
  req F-6.2: The enrich cascade (deterministic → classify → summarize → analyze) is idempotent
    and cancellable; each tier is individually invocable and capped.
  req F-6.3: The processing pipeline advances a durable cursor and can be reset.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Subscriptions
  req F-7.1: Bulk-mail senders are derived from the feed (List-Unsubscribe / body links) and
    listed for one-click unsubscribe + sender filtering.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Related content
  req F-8.1: People and organizations surface their related messages, events, and contacts via
    Related-role surfaces.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Sync Gmail into mailbox
  given: a mailbox bound to a Gmail connection
  when: sync runs (locally or on EDGE)
  then:
    - new messages appear in the feed, deduped and tagged with canonical system tags
    - re-running sync adds nothing (idempotent)
```

```mdl
test T-2: Save and apply filter
  given: a mailbox with tagged messages
  when: the user types a filter and saves it
  then:
    - a saved-filter node appears under the mailbox and reopens the filtered view
```

```mdl
test T-3: Draft, send, reconcile
  given: an open message
  when: the user replies and sends
  then:
    - the draft leaves Drafts; the sent copy appears via sync; no duplicates
```

```mdl
test T-4: Reading chain
  given: a mailbox plank with messages
  when: the user opens message A then message B
  then:
    - one message plank is reused; meta-click opens a second plank
```

```mdl
test T-5: Enrich cascade
  given: a synced mailbox
  when: enrich runs (or its routine fires)
  then:
    - classifications, summaries, and facts appear; re-running is a no-op; stop cancels cleanly
```

```mdl
test T-6: Draft event round-trip
  given: a calendar bound to Google
  when: the user creates and saves a draft event
  then:
    - the remote event is created and the next sync reconciles the local draft
```

```mdl
test T-7: Interactive during initial sync
  given: an empty mailbox starting its first sync
  then:
    - the article stays interactive and never flashes an empty state once messages exist
```

```mdl
test T-8: Unsubscribe
  given: a bulk-mail sender in Subscriptions
  when: the user unsubscribes
  then:
    - the RFC 8058 endpoint fires and a sender filter hides existing mail
```

---

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Add a mailbox, compose a draft, read it back
  desc: The core inbox round-trip — add a Mailbox, compose a local draft into it, then read the
    feed back. plugin-inbox is ON by default; no enabling step is required.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-4.1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - no Mailbox named "QA Mailbox" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Add the mailbox
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Mailbox. Name it "QA Mailbox".
      expect: a Mailbox named "QA Mailbox" appears under the collection, with an empty message list
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — `SpaceCapabilities.CreateObjectEntry` calls `Mailbox.make(props)` (which
        provisions the backing feed/tags/filters) before invoking `[op:addMailbox]`; passing a
        plain `{ name }` literal straight to `[op:addMailbox]` skips that factory and produces an
        object `draftEmail` cannot use (`Mailbox.make`'s feed/tags/filters are absent). The agent
        path re-resolves the mailbox from ECHO in each later step instead of capturing it here.
    - name: Compose a draft into it
      do: Click Compose from the mailbox toolbar, address it to "qa@example.com", subject "QA Draft", and a short body.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.inbox.draftEmail {
          subject: "QA Draft", to: "qa@example.com", body: "A QA round-trip.",
          mailbox: (await space.db.query(dxos.Filter.type(Mailbox)).run()).objects.find((m) => m.name === 'QA Mailbox')
        }
      capture: drafted
      expect: "QA Draft" appears at the top of the message list (newest-first) as a draft
      assert: return !!$drafted.newMessageDXN
    - name: Read the mailbox back
      do: Select "QA Draft" in the message list and confirm the reading pane shows the body.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.inbox.readEmail {
          mailbox: (await space.db.query(dxos.Filter.type(Mailbox)).run()).objects.find((m) => m.name === 'QA Mailbox'),
          limit: 5
        }
      expect: the returned payload includes the "QA Draft" subject and its body text
      assert: return $result.content.includes('QA Draft') && $result.content.includes('A QA round-trip.');
  after:
    - name: Delete the mailbox
      do: Right-click "QA Mailbox" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects {
          objects: [(await space.db.query(dxos.Filter.type(Mailbox)).run()).objects.find((m) => m.name === 'QA Mailbox') ?? (() => { throw new Error("Mailbox QA Mailbox not found — refusing to remove an unrelated object"); })()],
          target: $given.collection
        }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Create a draft calendar event and save it to Google
  desc: The two-way calendar round-trip. Blocked end-to-end without a live Google Connection —
    op:syncDraftEvents makes a real Google Calendar API call, which no fixture in this repo can
    stand up. Steps that only touch local ECHO state still run.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-5.1]
  status: blocked
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - a Calendar exists in the space (added the same way a Mailbox is, via the collection + create menu)
    - no draft event named "QA Event" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create a draft event
      do: On the CalendarArticle toolbar, click "Create event", name it "QA Event", set a start/end time.
      expect: a draft Event named "QA Event" appears on the grid, editable in EventArticle, with a Save action shown
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — createEvent is a component action (db-local, parented to the Calendar), not a
        declared op; describing it via `[op:...]` would name something that does not exist.
    - name: Save it to Google Calendar
      do: Click Save in EventArticle (or "Save events to calendar" on the toolbar).
      expect: the event round-trips to Google Calendar and the local draft is replaced by the synced feed copy
      blocked: |
        Requires a live Google Connection with the calendar.events scope and reachable Google
        Calendar API — no such fixture exists in this repo's QA harness, and op:syncDraftEvents has
        no registered `key:` to invoke through the debug port even if one did. Running this step
        against a real account is a manual, human-only exercise; do not fabricate a Connection to
        "unblock" it.
  after:
    - name: Delete the event
      do: Right-click "QA Event" (or its synced copy) and choose Delete.
      expect: the event leaves the grid and, if synced, is removed from Google Calendar
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — op:deleteEvent and op:syncDraftEvents are documented in this spec but have no
        `key:` yet: no `org.dxos.operation.inbox.deleteEvent` / `.syncDraftEvents` was found registered
        in `src/types/InboxOperation.ts`. Guessing one would violate Execution Rule 6.
```

